      "writtenOn": "2013-07-15T19:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure what\u0027s the proper way to do extension. I was under the impression that we need to park the extensions in keystone/contrib. Disabling an extension simply means removing it from the pipeline.\n\nBut OS-TRUST didn\u0027t follow this pattern so I am not sure. But since OS-INHERIT have heavy dependency on the existing role schema so I don\u0027t have strong objection for mingling the code. But should the routers be in keystone/contrib then? I still prefer the pipeline approach. But I got a feeling I am minority on this one. :)",
      "revId": "4e19586108e5a29a2dc59676d5e4013edb000efd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
